{
  "_comment": [
    "What each tier of the test matrix runs. Read by tool/matrix/matrix.py.",
    "",
    "A tier has two halves. `desktop` runs the app's Linux build: no phone",
    "hardware, but it starts in seconds and reshapes itself, so one process",
    "walks every listed shape. `android` runs on emulators, where the",
    "platform is real: one shape per run, applied to the emulator from",
    "outside.",
    "",
    "An android group is expanded over avds x shapes x langs x settings and",
    "then sampled: `cross` keeps every combination, `pairwise` keeps the",
    "fewest runs in which every pair of values still meets at least once,",
    "`rotate` keeps every avd x shape x lang and cycles settings across them.",
    "Depth and breadth are deliberately not multiplied: the sweep goes wide,",
    "the flows that exercise a feature run once per Android version."
  ],
  "aliases": {
    "pulse-minimal-avd": "pulse",
    "ring-medium-avd": "ring",
    "full-avd": "full"
  },
  "tiers": {
    "pulse": {
      "about": "Every change. One emulator, the screens people live in, every phone shape on the desktop build.",
      "desktop": [
        {
          "langs": ["ro"], "settings": ["default"],
          "shapes": ["phone_small", "phone_common", "phone_landscape", "tablet_portrait", "phone_large_text"],
          "flows": ["smoke", "sweep_core"]
        },
        {
          "langs": ["en"], "settings": ["busy"],
          "shapes": ["phone_small", "phone_large_text"],
          "flows": ["sweep_core"]
        }
      ],
      "android": [
        {
          "avds": ["speleo_mx_api34"],
          "shapes": ["native"], "langs": ["ro"], "settings": ["default"],
          "flows": ["smoke", "sweep_core", "trip_media"], "media": true,
          "sample": "cross"
        }
      ]
    },
    "ring": {
